course: dictionary
lesson: 7100
title: Peafowl: males, females and babies
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A peafowl is a large bird from the pheasant family. Its names work like a family: the male is a peacock, the female is a peahen, and the babies are peachicks. People often say peafowl for the whole group.
explain: The science lesson gives you clues. The peacock has a long, colourful tail with «eye» spots, and he fans it out to attract peahens. The peahen is brown and plain. So bright and showy means male, and brown and plain means female.
explain: Read this sentence in context: «The Congo peafowl, a shy cousin of the Indian peacock, lives only in the Congo forest.» Shy and only in the forest are clues that this bird is hard to spot. Cousin means a related bird, not the same bird. Swap in your own meaning to check it still makes sense.
fact: A peafowl is a large bird of the pheasant family.
fact: The male peafowl is called a peacock, and the female is called a peahen.
fact: A baby peafowl is called a peachick.
fact: The peacock fans out his tail, with «eye» spots, to attract peahens.
fact: The Indian peafowl is India's national bird.
exercise: What is the male peafowl called? | Peachick | Peahen | Peafowl | *Peacock
exercise: «The peacock fanned out his long, colourful tail.» Why does he do this? | To scare away the rain | To hide from a fox | *To attract a peahen | To keep his feet warm
exercise: Which phrase names a group of peafowl? | a herd of cows | a swarm of bees | *a flock of peafowl | a pride
test: Which bird has the long, colourful tail with «eye» spots? | *Peacock | Peachick | Peahen | Peafowl
test: «The Congo peafowl... lives only in the Congo forest.» Where does it live? | In India | In every zoo in the world | On farms in Scotland | *Only in the Congo forest
exam: What is the correct pairing? | *A peacock is the male, a peahen is the female, and a peachick is a baby | A peachick is the father, a peafowl is the mother | A peahen is the male, a peacock is the female | Peafowl are small insects
